# FrostBSD "Kali-flavor" package set — FreeBSD pkg names.
#
# These reproduce Kali's security flavor from native FreeBSD ports. Verify each
# with `pkg search <name>` on your target release; the build installs best-effort
# and warns (does not abort) on any that have no port.
#
# Kali is Debian/Linux; some of its tools have NO clean BSD port. Known gaps are
# listed at the bottom — use the FreeBSD linux compat layer (linuxulator) or a
# Linux jail/VM for those, or accept the native equivalent.

# --- recon / scanning ---
nmap
masscan
zmap
dns2tcp
whatweb

# --- traffic / MITM ---
tcpdump
wireshark
tshark
ettercap
socat
tcpreplay
hping3

# --- web ---
nikto
sqlmap
gobuster
ffuf
wfuzz

# --- passwords / cracking ---
hydra
john
hashcat
hashid

# --- wireless ---
aircrack-ng

# --- reversing / forensics ---
radare2
binwalk
yara
foremost
sleuthkit

# --- exploitation frameworks / libs ---
py-impacket
# (Metasploit: no reliable FreeBSD port — see gaps below)

# --- privacy / crypto ---
tor
gnupg
wireguard-tools
openvpn

# --- base workstation tooling ---
bash
sudo
doas
tmux
vim
git
curl
wget
python3

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# KNOWN GAPS (no clean native FreeBSD port as of writing — handle explicitly):
#   metasploit    -> run in a Linux jail/VM, or linuxulator (fragile)
#   burpsuite     -> Java app; install manually from vendor, not via pkg
#   responder     -> Python; pip install in a venv, verify BSD compatibility
#   bettercap     -> check net/bettercap; may lag Linux features
#   set (SET)     -> Social-Engineer Toolkit; Linux-oriented, use a VM
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
